  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1117 AM CDT Fri Jun 12 2026\n\nA short-wave trough will approach from the Plains Saturday night\ninto Sunday, increasing moisture and instability. Scattered\nshowers and thunderstorms will return, becoming more widespread\nSunday afternoon as another cold front moves south into Middle TN.\nMarginal shear and CAPE support a low chance for stronger storms,\nmainly across the southern and eastern areas. Primary threats\nremain gusty winds and heavy rainfall. \n\nCooler and drier air filters in behind the front early next week,\nbrining a pleasant stretch with highs in the upper 70s to lower\n80s and dew points retreating to the upper 50s. Rain chances will\nbe much lower Monday through Wednesday. \n\nMoisture returns mid to late week as high pressure shifts, with\nhighs climbing back into the upper 80s to low 90s by\nThursday/Friday. Upper-level flow remains weak, with only low\nchances for diurnal storms toward the end of the period. No major\npattern changes are expected through this period.",
